    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where $ \\psi(g, A) $ is the penetrance for an individual with this genotype. Substituting this likelihood into the previous mixed-model likelihoods (Equations 13.19–23) allows them to accommodate binary traits. For example, the likelihood $ \\ell(y | g_f, g_m, A_f, A_m) $ for a particular sib, conditioned on the major-locus genotypes and background polygenic values of its parents is",
