    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Segregation analysis proceeds by substituting this expression into Equation 13.29a. The resulting likelihood for the major-gene-only model has five parameters to estimate: the three major-locus means $ \\mu_{g} $, allele frequency q, and the threshold value T. (Alternatively, one can set T = 1 and estimate the variance of the liability function.) Examples of this general approach applied to several different genetic models can be found in Thaller et al. (1996).",
      "source_page": 392,
