    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "(Liao 1994). Hence, we can model the penetrance as a logistic function. For example, the penetrance for the major gene and polygenic background becomes $ \\psi(g, A) = f(a + \\alpha_g + \\alpha_A) $ where $ \\alpha_g $ and $ \\alpha_A $ are the effects of the major-locus genotype and polygenic background, and a is a term that accounts (among other things) for the general prevalence of the trait. Likewise, one can incorporate other factors (such as the effect of sex, specific environments, or specific age groups) as extra terms in the argument of logistic function.",
